WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.736
-The number-two House
Republican refused to say

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.373
that the 2020 election was
not stolen from Donald Trump,

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:09.408
while the Biden administration
blocked an attempt by Trump

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:11.744
to withhold documents related
to the investigation

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:14.614
of the January 6th
insurrection at the Capitol.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.083
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:22.588
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:24.357
There's a lot
going on right now,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.460
from the GOP's ongoing attempts
to dismantle democracy

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.563
to centrist Democrats holding up
President Biden's agenda

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:33.166
to Bernie Sanders
holding press conferences

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:35.534
in a leather chair,
therapist-style.

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.170
"How will we pay for it?

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.406
Oh! What a great question.
That is a new one!

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:41.907
I've never heard
that one before.

00:00:41.907 --> 00:00:45.711
I'm gonna write you a note
that says, 'Tax the rich,'

00:00:45.711 --> 00:00:48.114
and a prescription
for some ginkgo biloba."

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.215
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.450
But here's a moment
from last week

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.985
that pretty much sums
up my feelings

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.020
about the current state
of our politics.

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:56.022
Biden was asked about
a short-term deal

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.892
to avert economic catastrophe
and raise the debt ceiling.

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:01.261
In response,
he crossed his fingers,

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:02.795
although, at first,
I thought he was going

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.664
for a very different
hand gesture.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:15.541
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.044
It really does encapsulate
where we're at politically,

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.013
that every response
is a coin flip

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.582
between "hoping for the best"
and "[bleep] off!"

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:23.916
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:27.020
I definitely thought Biden
was going full bird there,

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:30.390
mostly because of his technique.
Yes, his fingers were crossed,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:33.126
but he brought it up like he was
cranking with the other hand.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.426
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:36.629
This was the risk we took

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.231
when we elected
President Finger Guns.

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:41.200
Those things
are deadly weapons.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:43.103
They make him run it
through the metal detector

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:45.071
when he comes to work
every morning.

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.472
With Trump,
I was always worried

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.574
he was going to say the wrong
thing to a world leader,

00:01:48.574 --> 00:01:50.810
but with Biden,
I'm afraid a hand gesture

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.779
is going to get away from him.
"Bad news --

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.513
The President tried to do
a 'I see you'

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.948
to the Sultan of Brunei,

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:57.984
and instead he slipped
and he Three Stooged him."

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.052
"What?!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.586
"Why didn't the Sultan
do a block hand?"

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.589
"I guess they don't
have the Stooges there."

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:04.257
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.458
During the time you were gone,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.394
we did a lot of
"MASH" references,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.997
a "Star Trek Next Generation,"

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.331
but obviously now
human beings are here.

00:02:12.331 --> 00:02:14.734
We had to freshen it up
with the Stooges.

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:17.570
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.372
While Biden was desperately
trying to convince Republicans

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:23.542
to do the bare minimum to avert
potential economic catastrophe

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.844
over the debt ceiling,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:27.279
he was also refusing
an attempt by his predecessor

00:02:27.279 --> 00:02:29.982
to shield documents from
a congressional investigation

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.318
into the insurrection
on January 6th.

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:35.054
-NBC News first to report
earlier today

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.124
that the Biden White House
has decided, in fact,

00:02:38.124 --> 00:02:41.327
not to block the release
of documents related to Trump,

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.996
his presidency,
and the insurrection.

00:02:43.996 --> 00:02:48.234
The move sets up a legal
and potentially lengthy showdown

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:51.003
between two presidents,
current and former,

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.406
over the issue
of executive privilege.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.942
-The White House is blocking
former President Trump

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.311
from playing
the executive privilege card,

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:01.915
and the committee investigating
the January 6th insurrection

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:03.516
says Donald Trump's minions

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:06.719
will not get away
with ignoring the rule of law.

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:09.022
-Okay. Now that's definitely
a middle finger.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.657
So Trump thought he could
just unilaterally

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:14.393
assert executive privilege,
no questions asked.

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:16.262
You're not president
anymore, dude.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.264
That's not how it works.
What's he gonna do next?

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.499
Try to book a flight
on Air Force One?

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.268
"What do you mean
I can't use the plane anymore?

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:25.838
But what about all those miles
I racked up?

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.373
Can I transfer them to JetBlue?

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.409
JetBlue.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.244
We love JetBlue,
don't we, folks?"

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:32.412
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.614
"JetBlue, the first place
I ever had a Terra chip,

00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:37.550
and I remember --"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.252
I remember,
I said to the stewardess,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:42.621
"There's something wrong
with my chip -- it's red.

00:03:42.621 --> 00:03:44.057
I have a red chip."

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.192
And she told me, she said to me,
"Sir" -- tears in her eyes --

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:50.496
she said, 'Sir, that's
a seasonal root vegetable.'"

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.598
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.435
Now, before we dive into
that story any further --

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.802
the executive-privilege story --

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:58.604
not the Trump, JetBlue,
Terra chip story.

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:01.441
I think we got all
we're gonna get from that.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:05.311
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:08.314
And they said we couldn't do
tangents when the audience came.

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.983
We're gonna do --
gonna take a few tangents.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:14.720
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.256
I do think it's worth taking
a quick step back to acknowledge

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:19.424
this is our first show with
a live audience in 19 months.

00:04:19.424 --> 00:04:22.327
Well, to be fair, we did have
a full audience one night

00:04:22.327 --> 00:04:24.096
this summer, but they didn't
laugh at anything,

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.364
so we just pretended
they weren't there

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:27.266
and decided to wait a while
before trying again.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:29.268
It's been a long,
strange trip.

00:04:29.268 --> 00:04:31.704
We did a show in my attic,
in my in-laws house,

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.273
I befriended Ethan Hawke
and a painting of a sea captain,

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.441
I grew my hair out,

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:38.377
and I started dressing
casually -- by choice --

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:40.112
and not,
as "The Daily Mail" reported,

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:41.914
because I had to sell my suits

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.817
to cover gambling losses
incurred

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:48.020
when I took me under on the Mets
having one [bleep] season.

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:49.622
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.190
Second Mets joke.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.391
First one is in the monologue,

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:55.228
so if you only watch
this online,

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:57.863
you gotta go back
and watch the monologue now.

00:04:57.863 --> 00:04:59.264
What's that?
You're not going to?

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:02.134
Because you live in Austria
and you hate the Mets jokes?

00:05:02.134 --> 00:05:05.104
Fair enough.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:07.573
Over the last 19 months,
I became closer with my crew,

00:05:07.573 --> 00:05:09.375
who were the only feedback
I had in real time.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.010
Speaking of the crew...

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.612
Oh!
Oh, that's very interesting,

00:05:13.612 --> 00:05:14.981
because earlier today,
Wally said,

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:16.382
"I bet the first time
you cut to me,

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.584
I'll get a round of applause
from the audience and yet --

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:22.088
[ Cheers and applause ]
Doesn't count! Doesn't count!

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:25.758
It doesn't count.
No, no, no!

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.860
No, no, no! It doesn't count
'cause he didn't do anything.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.262
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:30.697
You did nothing!
When we cut to him,

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.265
you did nothing, and I had to
say it, and then you did it,

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.899
so it doesn't count!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.135
Doesn't count, Wally.
-That was too fast of a cut!

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:38.070
-You didn't stipulate
how fast the cut would be!

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.471
-This is an outrage!
-Outrage!

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:41.240
Oh, we spent
so much time together,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:42.942
we finish
each other's sentences.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:49.181
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.750
The point is...

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.953
right up until you gave Wally
what he wanted,

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.555
I'm thrilled to be back
in front of an audience.

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.055
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.055 --> 00:05:59.425
And I'm just hoping my audience
is a little more enthusiastic

00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:01.961
than Trump's audience.
The man just refuses to go away.

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:04.831
On Saturday, he went to Iowa
to hold yet another rally

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.465
where he repeated
the same deranged lies

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:08.400
about the election that
he's been repeating for months.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:11.303
And yet even his own crowd
wasn't exactly electrified

00:06:11.303 --> 00:06:13.606
by hearing the same old
incoherent nonsense

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:16.109
over and over again.
-You know, I was up by

00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:20.412
massive numbers on Election Day.

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:23.248
It was even --
The news was saying, "Wow.

00:06:23.248 --> 00:06:24.683
What a big lead
in Pennsylvania."

00:06:24.683 --> 00:06:25.851
I love Pennsylvania.

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:29.154
I went to school
in Pennsylvania -- college.

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:32.257
But what a great state
and what great people.

00:06:32.257 --> 00:06:33.693
And I was up by so much.

00:06:33.693 --> 00:06:37.229
All of a sudden,
the booths close,

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:39.498
the tabulation centers
are closed,

00:06:39.498 --> 00:06:41.367
3:00 in the morning.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:45.771
And shortly thereafter, we tied.

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:48.207
They know they got caught.

00:06:48.207 --> 00:06:51.710
All you have to do
is listen to the numbers.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.712
And remember what I said.

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:58.150
Joe Biden has launched a foreign
invasion of his own country.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.654
"Come on in."
He said, "Come in."

00:07:01.654 --> 00:07:03.823
This is a, uh --
This is a sick --

00:07:03.823 --> 00:07:06.558
This is a sick thing
that's happening to our country.

00:07:06.558 --> 00:07:09.462
-Wow. And I was worried about
bringing audiences back.

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:10.663
[ Laughter ]

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:11.764
I never thought I'd say this,

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.399
but maybe you should go
into lockdown.

00:07:13.399 --> 00:07:15.100
You know, remote shows
might be better for you.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.703
You could borrow my attic.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:19.572
Although,
if you were in my attic,

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.841
I'd never get any sleep.
"Honey, what's that noise?"

00:07:21.841 --> 00:07:24.610
"I think he's talking about
how windmills kill birds."

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.045
"It's 2:00 --
2:00 in the morning."

00:07:27.045 --> 00:07:29.148
"I know, but he had
like 50 Diet Cokes."

00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:31.017
[ Laughter ]

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:33.018
"Why did you let him
use our attic?"

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:34.387
"Because he used
to be president!

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:37.156
I'm sorry that
I respect the office!"

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:39.992
Also, I love the cutaways
to sullen Trump fans

00:07:39.992 --> 00:07:41.327
just standing there
in silence,

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.795
like tourists watching one
of those gold-statue guys

00:07:43.795 --> 00:07:45.697
in Times Square.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.697 --> 00:07:49.402
"So, is he gonna like...
do something?"

00:07:49.402 --> 00:07:50.436
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.436 --> 00:07:52.004
And you could tell
Trump was waiting

00:07:52.004 --> 00:07:53.773
for a crowd reaction, too.
I mean, look at him.

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:57.743
It's like watching a open-mic
night at the senior center.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:01.914
"Joe Biden said, 'Come on in.
Come on in.' Am I right?"

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.749
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.418
"Cyrus knows
what I'm talking about."

00:08:05.418 --> 00:08:07.153
[ Laughter ]

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:09.655
"Cyrus?"
[ Laughter ]

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:11.757
"Cyrus."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:13.426
"Get the paddles.
What else?"

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:14.794
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.794 --> 00:08:17.363
It's been liberating
not having to think or care

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:19.899
about what this lunatic says
or does on a daily basis

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:21.633
for the last few months.
Unfortunately, the GOP

00:08:21.633 --> 00:08:23.435
has not felt the same way.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.204
They're still
fully devoted to Trump.

00:08:25.204 --> 00:08:27.973
He was joined at his rally
by Iowa Senator Chuck Grassley.

00:08:27.973 --> 00:08:29.809
Virtually the entirety
of the Republican Party

00:08:29.809 --> 00:08:32.745
remains in thrall to Trump
and committed to the Big Lie

00:08:32.745 --> 00:08:34.480
that the election was
somehow stolen from him,

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.449
as demonstrated
by this interview,

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:38.484
the number-two House
Republican Steve Scalise did

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:39.985
on Fox News Sunday.

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:45.891
-Do you think the 2020 election
was stolen from Donald Trump?

00:08:45.891 --> 00:08:48.760
And continuing
to make that charge.

00:08:48.760 --> 00:08:52.063
Not having states
do election reforms

00:08:52.063 --> 00:08:54.266
but specifically
making this charge

00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:56.335
that the election was stolen.

00:08:56.335 --> 00:09:01.874
Do you think that that hurts,
undermines American democracy?

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:03.742
-Well, Chris, I've been very
clear from the beginning.

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:05.210
If you look
at a number of states,

00:09:05.210 --> 00:09:07.680
they didn't follow
their state-passed laws.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.348
-The states all certified --
-They didn't follow

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:10.716
those legislative rules.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:12.051
Right.
But at the end of the day,

00:09:12.051 --> 00:09:14.787
are we gonna follow
what the Constitution says?

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:17.122
-Do you think the election
was stolen or not?

00:09:17.122 --> 00:09:18.924
I understand you think
there were irregularities

00:09:18.924 --> 00:09:20.693
and things that need
to be fixed.

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:22.361
Do you think
the election was stolen?

00:09:22.361 --> 00:09:25.131
-And it's not just irregular.
It's states that did not follow

00:09:25.131 --> 00:09:27.233
the laws set,
which the Constitution

00:09:27.233 --> 00:09:28.701
says they're supposed to follow.

00:09:28.701 --> 00:09:30.902
-I like how they say
the word "irregularities"

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:32.904
without actually specifying
what that means.

00:09:32.904 --> 00:09:35.841
It's that vague Mafia talk
they've all adopted.

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:37.376
"It's a shame what happened
to your restaurant,

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:38.811
but the boss
got your last payment,

00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:41.147
and there was some, uh,
irregularities."

00:09:41.147 --> 00:09:42.614
[ Laughter ]

00:09:42.614 --> 00:09:45.083
These guys can't actually give
an example of widespread fraud

00:09:45.083 --> 00:09:46.952
because there aren't any,
as multiple audits

00:09:46.952 --> 00:09:48.420
and roughly 60 court cases,

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:51.457
including with several
Trump-appointed judges, proved.

00:09:51.457 --> 00:09:54.760
But all they have are these bat
[bleep] conspiracy theories

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.695
promoted by the rotating
cast of weirdos

00:09:56.695 --> 00:09:59.431
who inhabit Trump's orbit,
rambling incoherently

00:09:59.431 --> 00:10:01.300
about nonsense
like Italian satellites,

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:03.268
hacking voting machines,
or mysterious midnight

00:10:03.268 --> 00:10:06.005
election dumps or bamboo
fibers on ballots.

00:10:06.005 --> 00:10:08.474
Last week,
MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell

00:10:08.474 --> 00:10:10.375
once again repeated
the insane claim

00:10:10.375 --> 00:10:12.078
that dead people
had somehow voted.

00:10:12.078 --> 00:10:13.846
-I'll give an example today.

00:10:13.846 --> 00:10:20.052
2,650 people
over the age of 100.

00:10:20.052 --> 00:10:22.187
Now, you might say,
"Oh, wow. That's --

00:10:22.187 --> 00:10:24.557
That could be, that could be.

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:27.059
2,000 of them were over 200.

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:30.629
Wouldn't you like
to live in that state?

00:10:30.629 --> 00:10:33.031
Brad, they were
200-and-some years old,

00:10:33.031 --> 00:10:35.634
so obviously they
one guy was --

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:37.803
